### 1. `.github/workflows/build.yml` (GitHub Actions)

```yaml
name: Nova AI Singularity Build

on:
  push:
    branches: [ main, develop ]
    tags: ['v*']
  workflow_dispatch:

env:
  GRADLE_OPTS: -Dorg.gradle.daemon=false -Dorg.gradle.parallel=true

jobs:
  build-apk:
    name: 🏗️ Build Debug APK
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    
    steps:
      - name: Checkout code
        uses: actions/checkout@v4
        
      - name: Set up JDK 17
        uses: actions/setup-java@v4
        with:
          java-version: '17'
          distribution: 'temurin'
          cache: gradle
          
      - name: Grant execute permission for gradlew
        run: chmod +x gradlew
        
      - name: Build Debug APK
        run: ./gradlew assembleDebug --stacktrace --no-daemon
        
      - name: Rename APK with commit SHA
        run: |
          COMMIT_SHA=${GITHUB_SHA::7}
          mv app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk \
             nova-ai-debug-${COMMIT_SHA}.apk
             
      - name: Upload APK Artifact
        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: nova-apk-debug-${{ github.sha }}
          path: nova-ai-debug-*.apk
          retention-days: 30
          
      - name: Create GitHub Release (if tagged)
        if: startsWith(github.ref, 'refs/tags/v')
        uses: softprops/action-gh-release@v1
        with:
          files: nova-ai-debug-*.apk
          body: |
            ## Nova AI Singularity Edition ${{ github.ref_name }}
            
            Automated build from commit ${{ github.sha }}
            
            ### 📥 Installation Steps
            1. Download APK from assets below
            2. Transfer to Android device
            3. Enable "Install from Unknown Sources" in Settings → Security
            4. Open APK file and tap Install
            5. Launch Nova AI and configure API keys in Settings
            
            ### ⚙️ Required Permissions (grant after install)
            - Accessibility Service (for device control)
            - Notification Access (for reading notifications aloud)
            - Camera & Microphone (for AR vision and voice input)
            - Location (for predictive suggestions)
            
            ### 🔑 API Keys Configuration
            After installation, open app → Settings (gear icon):
            - Gemini API Key: Get free key from https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
            - OpenAI Key (optional): For ChatGPT integration
            - Anthropic Key (optional): For Claude integration
            
            ### ✨ Phase 10 Features Included
            - Living Quantum Orb UI with audio-reactive particles
            - Multi-LLM failover (Gemini → OpenRouter → Local → Fallback)
            - Cross-AI interoperability (talk to ChatGPT/Claude simultaneously)
            - Distributed cognition (hive mind parallel research)
            - Self-awareness simulation (meta-cognition dashboard)
            - Universal translator (earbud mode + AR overlay)
            - Autonomous UI agent with safety gates
            - Predictive intent engine
            - Biometric mood fusion
            - Privacy-preserving federated learning
            
            ---
            Built with ❤️ by Nova AI Team
        env:
          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
